                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient shows a significantly elevated PSA level (14.6 ng/mL; normal 0–4 ng/mL), which is unexpected in a 62-year-old female, as PSA is typically associated with prostate tissue. This result may indicate a preanalytical or clerical error, or rare ectopic PSA production. Recommend verification of patient identity, sample labeling, and clinical correlation.</td>
